        "question": "Why do thin borders around the edge of a business card often look uneven when printed?",
        "answer": "Commercial hydraulic paper guillotines cut stacks of 500 sheets at high pressure and have a mechanical tolerance of ±0.5mm to 1mm. A thin 2mm border frame makes even a 0.5mm shift look visually lopsided. Always avoid thin perimeter frames or make borders at least 5mm thick.",
        "is_approved": true
